{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULING (recorded verbatim, attributed to the operator): \"review-code should not require a config key to be active. It should operate comparably to plan review: a config key controls whether it is REQUIRED, not whether it is AVAILABLE. Making it required is out of scope for this bug; dropping the config key gating availability is approved.\" — Proceeding under this ruling: only the explicit CLI/library/MCP review-code surface loses the availability gate; gate-triggered/automatic call sites keep their current enablement behavior; no enforcement semantics are added."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787334402521251001,"uuid":"73398b9a-037a-4e96-85c7-aed7653c1bee"}